HARDWARE MATRIX ACCELERATION (AMX / SME)\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 A. Intel AMX (Advanced Matrix Extensions)\
Utilizes Tile registers (TMM).\
Operation: C[i][j] += Sum(k=0 to K-1) [A[i][k] * B[k][j]]\
One 'tdpbusd' instruction performs hundreds of int8 ops per cycle, providing the "10x" leap over scalar code.\
B. ARM SME (Scalable Matrix Extension)\
Uses the Outer Product: ZA += P * Q^T. This is critical for high-efficiency AI inference on Apple Silicon and ARM Neoverse servers.\
